FILE: stale.rs
MOD: commands/stale
OWNS: composite health check — sequences validate + coverage + drift into one command
PROFILE: [io]
CHANGE-FREQUENCY: volatile

run: bool → Result<(), String> [io, boundary]
  calls: ArchContext::load, validate::check, coverage::check, drift::check
  note: section headers [validate]/[coverage]/[drift] only printed when that section has issues

CNTR: stale::run ↔ validate::check: ValidationResult fields (errors, warnings, container_count) must stay in sync — stale uses them directly
CNTR: stale::run ↔ coverage::check: CoverageResult.unmapped field must stay Vec<String> — stale iterates it directly
CNTR: stale::run ↔ drift::check: DriftResult + DriftItem fields (items, scanned_count, kind) must stay in sync — stale filters by kind=="forbidden"
CNTR: stale::run ↔ drift::DriftItem: field names (module_id, file, import_raw, line_number, target_module, kind) serialized directly into stale JSON

DEPENDS-ON: context, commands/validate, commands/coverage, commands/drift

KEY-INVARIANTS:
- exit code 1 on validate errors OR drift forbidden violations; unmapped files and undeclared deps are warnings (exit 0) — matches standalone command behaviour
- stale is explicitly excluded from commands-isolation fitness rules — it is the only command that legitimately imports peers

